    "https://centralmethodist.libguides.com/c.php?g=1403531": {
      "title": "Meet the Staff - Director - Cindy Rogan '25, Director of Career Development",
      "description": "Home - Career Development Center - LibGuides at Central Methodist University Skip to Main Content Smiley Memorial Library CMU Website | Ask a Librarian ▾ Email Us Call Us Chat With a Librarian Central Methodist University LibGuides Career Development Center Home Search this Guide Search Career Development Center: Home Resource for resumes, cover letters, interview skills, graduate school, interview skills, and job search. Home Resume Cover Letter Work Study, Internship, Job Search Internships Graduate School Networking Interview Skills Career Counseling Employer Connect Career Information by Major Welcome to the James C. Denneny, Jr. Career Development Center At the James C. Denneny Jr. Career Development Center, our mission is to empower students as they build the skills, confidence, and professional readiness needed to successfully transition from college to career. We support both students and alumni through personalized services—including résumé reviews, career planning, job and internship search assistance, and more. We are open Monday through Friday, 8 a.m. to 4 p.m. Visit us on the second floor of the Inman Student and Community Center , or reach out anytime at career@centralmethodist.edu —we’re here to help you take the next step toward your future. Meet the Staff - Director - Cindy Rogan '25, Director of Career Development I serve as the Director of Career Services at Central Methodist University, where I enjoy helping students explore their interests and plan their next steps after graduation. With experience in higher education and nonprofit leadership, I believe career development works best when it is collaborative, practical, and personal. Before joining Career Services, I worked in Advancement and Alumni Relations at Central, leading programs and managing scholarship partnerships while collaborating with faculty, staff, alumni, and community partners to support student success. I also bring several years of leadership experience from my work with Birth It Forward, a Kansas City–area nonprofit focused on community support and program development. The Career Center has a wealth of resources available for our students and alumni, and we hope that you will take advantage of each of them. Take a moment to browse the page and explore the many options available to you.  If you have any questions, please feel free to stop by our office or email us at career@centralmethodist.edu . Meet the Staff - Administrative Assistant - Nichole Atkins Hello and welcome to the Central Methodist University James C. Denney, Jr. Career Development Center! I am Nichole and I am the newest member of the James C. Denney, Jr. Career Development Center team.  I bring more than 10 years of diverse management, entrepreneurship, and leadership experience. I am thrilled to help CMU students unlock their potential and build thriving careers. As a local business owner, I already share a deep bond with the local community and am excited to support the Eagle family in this next chapter. If I am not in my office helping students prep for their futures, I’m planning my next travel adventure, diving into a good book, relaxing with my dogs, or enjoying a great cup of coffee. Stop by the Career Development Center to say hello or send us an email!  I am excited to help you soar to new beginnings and an amazing future career. Next: Resume >> Last Updated: Aug 17, 2026 1:41 PM URL: https://centralmethodist.libguides.com/c.php?g=1403531 Print Page Login to LibApps Subjects: Career & Professional Development Smiley Memorial Library 411 Central Methodist Square Fayette, MO 65248 Phone: +1 (660) 248-6271 Email: library@centralmethodist.edu Quick Links Report an Issue with a Guide Smiley Memorial Library Catalog Course Reserves Contact Us Connect With Us Facebook Instagram Snapchat Smiley Memorial Library • Central Methodist University"
    },
